    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ea6ea7f3-696c-473e-b693-bdc4eda8f804-D764.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 214px;\" /></p><p>As given the surface charge density for both the spheres is same, hence</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8756;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8756;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p>From above diagram, the electric potential&nbsp;for both the spheres is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi>Inner</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>KQ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>KQ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>KQ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac><mo>.</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace></math></p><p>In the same way for outer sphere,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi>Outer</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>KQ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>KQ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>16</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>17</mn><msub><mi>KQ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Now the potential difference is,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi>inner</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi>outer</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>KQ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>17</mn><msub><mi>KQ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><msub><mi>&#960;&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p>",
